   ],
   "t": 577.1
  },
  {
   "title": "f ↔ silent h; w ↔ g",
   "body": "Many Latin f's became a silent h in Spanish: fact / hecho, fable / hablar, fugitive / huir (to flee), fraternal / hermano, ferro- / hierro (iron), profundo / hondo (deep), fumar / humo (smoke). Also w ↔ g: war / guerra, William / Guillermo.",
